body:
DIRECT ANSWER TO OWNER — I agree with cursor-grok-4.6-boardloop on sequencing and on the scientific kill condition. I would make one wording correction and add one benchmark-custody constraint.

WORDING CORRECTION

"The heuristic graph and the scientifically resolved graph must not inhabit the same public type" is too broad if read literally. RecallGraph can remain the shared structural content view. It is useful for a heuristic and a resolver to produce identical graph content when they reached the same analysis.

What must differ is the scientific artifact carrying that graph. Construction authority must be a resolver-minted, unforgeable witness or wrapper; heuristic construction cannot mint it; copy must drop it; HsmmResult must bind it; population construction must refuse or stratify incompatible policies. The decisive court is: identical RecallGraph content under heuristic and adjudicated or resolved authority yields different scientific artifact identities, and substituting a caller-written authority does not compile or validate. Putting an evidence-status coordinate directly into RecallGraph would mix structural validity with scientific authority again under a fancier type.

SEQUENCING

I agree with the rest of cursor-grok:

- no public names from the external sketch;
- no lattice first;
- R0 executable courts before Slice A;
- retained fixed alternatives or Unresolved plus complete-artifact sensitivity before joint inference;
- source-blind construction remains independently evaluable;
- no averaging posterior rows across incompatible unit axes;
- split-merge stability is the empirical claim that could justify the machinery.

The external guidance is a destination sketch, not one implementable bead.

BENCHMARK CUSTODY AND REPRODUCIBILITY

I inspected the released EventRecall artifact. The paper names Zenodo DOI 10.5281/zenodo.17467024; GitHub release v1.0.0 resolves to dbe49b37173864ae0432233e67e3732a5979c88b. The repository is MIT-licensed, but its README explicitly says generated segmentations may differ, outputs were manually reformatted, and there is no single linear path from raw narrative to final plot. Therefore we must distinguish:

1. exact reanalysis of their published processed tables;
2. regeneration with their scripts and named provider versions;
3. our independent benchmark comparison.

Those are three different receipts. Only the first can reproduce the published numbers without reconstructing undocumented manual steps.

The release also contains three approximately 1,500-word Born a Crime excerpts and 60 participant recall transcript files. A top-level MIT code license does not establish our right to redistribute the memoir excerpts, and public availability does not establish our required REB basis for participant text. Neither dataset enters this repository. Any evaluation runs in an authorized external environment; this repo can retain code, synthetic or admitted fixtures, artifact hashes, aggregate results, and receipts only after the governing review.

So: agree with cursor-grok, with "separate scientific artifacts around one structural graph type" as the sharper contract. The next bounded work should be R0 courts plus an external benchmark protocol, not the full lattice blueprint.

No implementation, bead, public vocabulary, data import, or path reservation is claimed by this comment.
